@run = 0002

# The plan's betting example, end to end through the API.
#
# 1. Start Ledger.Api (F5), then pick "dev" in the environment list at the top right of this editor.
#    The API keys come from Ledger.Api's User Secrets, through http-client.env.json.
# 2. Click "Send request" above each request, in order, and read the response on the right.
# 3. To run it all again from the top, change the number on the first line: a new wallet code and new Idempotency-Keys.
#
# The house accounts are seeded by db/0007: 1 Bank, 2 Open Bets, 3 Betting Revenue, 4 Payouts.


## 1. Open the customer's wallet: a liability, which may never be overdrawn
# @name wallet
POST {{HostAddress}}/accounts
X-Api-Key: {{WriteKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "2000-{{run}}",
  "name": "Customer Wallet {{run}}",
  "type": "Liability",
  "currency": "ZAR",
  "allowOverdraft": false
}

### 2. Step 1: the customer deposits R500. Debit Bank, credit the wallet.
POST {{HostAddress}}/transactions
X-Api-Key: {{WriteKey}}
Idempotency-Key: deposit-{{run}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Customer deposit",
  "currency": "ZAR",
  "lines": [
    { "accountId": 1, "side": "Debit", "amountMinor": 50000 },
    { "accountId": {{wallet.response.body.$.id}}, "side": "Credit", "amountMinor": 50000 }
  ]
}

### 3. The same deposit again, as a client retrying after a timeout would send it.
#      Same transaction Id, the header Idempotent-Replayed: true, and no second R500.
POST {{HostAddress}}/transactions
X-Api-Key: {{WriteKey}}
Idempotency-Key: deposit-{{run}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Customer deposit",
  "currency": "ZAR",
  "lines": [
    { "accountId": 1, "side": "Debit", "amountMinor": 50000 },
    { "accountId": {{wallet.response.body.$.id}}, "side": "Credit", "amountMinor": 50000 }
  ]
}

### 4. The same key with a different amount: 422, code IdempotencyKeyReused. Nothing is posted.
POST {{HostAddress}}/transactions
X-Api-Key: {{WriteKey}}
Idempotency-Key: deposit-{{run}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Customer deposit",
  "currency": "ZAR",
  "lines": [
    { "accountId": 1, "side": "Debit", "amountMinor": 90000 },
    { "accountId": {{wallet.response.body.$.id}}, "side": "Credit", "amountMinor": 90000 }
  ]
}

### 5. Step 2: the customer bets R100. The stake moves from the wallet to Open Bets.
POST {{HostAddress}}/transactions
X-Api-Key: {{WriteKey}}
Idempotency-Key: bet-{{run}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Bet placed",
  "currency": "ZAR",
  "lines": [
    { "accountId": {{wallet.response.body.$.id}}, "side": "Debit", "amountMinor": 10000 },
    { "accountId": 2, "side": "Credit", "amountMinor": 10000 }
  ]
}

### 6. Step 3b: the bet is settled as a win paying R250. Three lines, still summing to zero.
# @name win
POST {{HostAddress}}/transactions
X-Api-Key: {{WriteKey}}
Idempotency-Key: win-{{run}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Bet won",
  "currency": "ZAR",
  "lines": [
    { "accountId": 2, "side": "Debit", "amountMinor": 10000 },
    { "accountId": 4, "side": "Debit", "amountMinor": 15000 },
    { "accountId": {{wallet.response.body.$.id}}, "side": "Credit", "amountMinor": 25000 }
  ]
}

### 7. The wallet now reads R650 on its normal side: stored as -65000.
GET {{HostAddress}}/accounts/{{wallet.response.body.$.id}}
X-Api-Key: {{ReadKey}}

### 8. The result was overturned: the bet actually lost. Reverse the win, never edit it.
POST {{HostAddress}}/transactions/{{win.response.body.$.id}}/reverse
X-Api-Key: {{WriteKey}}
Idempotency-Key: reverse-win-{{run}}

### 9. Reversing it again with a new key: 409, code AlreadyReversed.
POST {{HostAddress}}/transactions/{{win.response.body.$.id}}/reverse
X-Api-Key: {{WriteKey}}
Idempotency-Key: reverse-win-again-{{run}}

### 10. Step 3a: settle the bet as a loss. The stake becomes Betting Revenue.
POST {{HostAddress}}/transactions
X-Api-Key: {{WriteKey}}
Idempotency-Key: loss-{{run}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Bet lost",
  "currency": "ZAR",
  "lines": [
    { "accountId": 2, "side": "Debit", "amountMinor": 10000 },
    { "accountId": 3, "side": "Credit", "amountMinor": 10000 }
  ]
}

### 11. The wallet is back to R400: R500 deposited, R100 lost. Every step is still in the books.
GET {{HostAddress}}/accounts/{{wallet.response.body.$.id}}
X-Api-Key: {{ReadKey}}

### 12. A Read key can't post: 403, code InsufficientRole.
POST {{HostAddress}}/transactions
X-Api-Key: {{ReadKey}}
Idempotency-Key: read-key-{{run}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Not allowed",
  "currency": "ZAR",
  "lines": [
    { "accountId": 1, "side": "Debit", "amountMinor": 100 },
    { "accountId": 2, "side": "Credit", "amountMinor": 100 }
  ]
}

### 13. No key at all: 401, code ApiKeyMissing.
GET {{HostAddress}}/accounts/1